WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.279 --> 00:00:03.795
- For somebody driving
into town the first time,

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:06.218
you wouldn't think there was a lot here

00:00:06.218 --> 00:00:10.734
because 95% of it is hiding underground.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:14.071
People drive in and go,
"Where is the place?

00:00:14.071 --> 00:00:16.019
"I don't understand."

00:00:16.019 --> 00:00:18.936
(didgeridoo music)

00:00:20.428 --> 00:00:25.227
Coober Pedy is from the
Aboriginal kupa-piti, which means

00:00:25.227 --> 00:00:26.894
white man in a hole.

00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:31.278
At the moment upstairs it is

00:00:31.278 --> 00:00:33.695
about 122 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:00:35.997 --> 00:00:40.594
Down here we're sitting
on about 71, 72 degrees.

00:00:40.594 --> 00:00:42.624
No air conditioner necessary.

00:00:42.624 --> 00:00:44.048
We're right out in the middle of nowhere.

00:00:44.048 --> 00:00:47.218
It takes a day to drive
here from Adelaide.

00:00:47.218 --> 00:00:51.042
I'd say there's about
1,000 underground dwellings

00:00:51.042 --> 00:00:54.709
and at least 1,500 people
living underground.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.953
(whistling)

00:00:57.953 --> 00:01:00.928
We've got five underground churches.

00:01:00.928 --> 00:01:03.364
We've got underground motels.

00:01:03.364 --> 00:01:06.773
There's some amazing
underground homes here,

00:01:06.773 --> 00:01:10.555
many bedrooms, underground
workshop, you name it underground

00:01:10.555 --> 00:01:12.638
we've pretty well got it.

00:01:15.196 --> 00:01:18.279
I bought my dugout as a fairly small

00:01:19.753 --> 00:01:22.233
two bedroom dugout and
I've been extending it

00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:23.454
over the years.

00:01:23.454 --> 00:01:28.341
Some of this I blasted out
when I could get away with it.

00:01:28.341 --> 00:01:30.414
The cops don't like us blasting in town.

00:01:30.414 --> 00:01:32.040
We don't do it anymore.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.700
Back in the old days, if
somebody was gonna have a baby,

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.012
we'd rock around there with
a couple of compressors

00:01:38.012 --> 00:01:40.875
on the weekend and some
jackhammers, and a couple of cartons

00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:44.128
of beer, and by the Sunday
night, we'd dug out a room,

00:01:44.128 --> 00:01:46.156
cemented the floor, and mired it up,

00:01:46.156 --> 00:01:49.489
and, um, there's your new baby's room, honey.

00:01:51.003 --> 00:01:54.670
Even though we're so
far away geographically

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.557
from anywhere else, I don't know why,

00:01:57.557 --> 00:02:00.474
but we just love the place to bits.

